<.docs_layout active_guide="sign-in">
  <.doc_heading
    title="Sign-in page"
    description="One sign-in page for every app that signs people in with Microsoft. It shows the application's name, Sign in with Microsoft, and what happened last. Development builds add a development sign-in. Phones get the form edge to edge, tablets a card, desktops a picture panel beside the form."
  />

  <div class="mt-10 space-y-12">
    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Desktop</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
        From 64rem. The left half names the application over the app's picture (or the primary
        colour in light, a card in dark, without one). The form is on the right.
      </p>
      <.preview_frame size="desktop" slug="signed-out" />
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Tablet and phone</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
        Tablets (40rem to 64rem) get the form in a card, over the picture when there is one.
        Phones (below 40rem) get it edge to edge. The button is 44px tall wherever touch is likely.
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-start gap-6">
        <.preview_frame size="tablet" slug="signed-out" />
        <.preview_frame size="phone" slug="signed-out" />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">States</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
        What happened last shows above the button. A refusal or a failure is red, anything else
        a plain notice. Pick a size to see every state at it.
      </p>
      <div role="tablist" class="tabs tabs-box w-fit">
        <input
          type="radio"
          name="sign-in-size"
          class="tab"
          aria-label="Phone"
          value="phone"
          checked
        />
        <input type="radio" name="sign-in-size" class="tab" aria-label="Tablet" value="tablet" />
        <input type="radio" name="sign-in-size" class="tab" aria-label="Desktop" value="desktop" />
      </div>
      <div id="sign-in-states" class="sign-in-states grid gap-6">
        <div :for={state <- ShadcnDaisyuiDemoWeb.SignInPreview.states()} class="space-y-2">
          <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-2">
            <h3 class="text-sm font-medium">{state.title}</h3>
            <a
              href={ShadcnDaisyuiDemoWeb.SignInPreview.path(state.slug)}
              class="text-xs text-muted-foreground underline-offset-4 hover:underline"
              target="_blank"
            >
              Open
            </a>
          </div>
          <div data-size="phone">
            <.preview_frame size="phone" slug={state.slug} scale="small" />
          </div>
          <div data-size="tablet">
            <.preview_frame size="tablet" slug={state.slug} scale="small" />
          </div>
          <div data-size="desktop">
            <.preview_frame size="desktop" slug={state.slug} scale="small" />
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Usage</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
        The page is the whole screen, so the sign-in template renders it on its own, outside <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm">Layouts.app/1</code>,
        with the flash group beside it. The app passes its own name, picture and routes.
      </p>
      <.code_block
        language="heex"
        code={
          ~S'''
          <.sign_in_page
            app_name="Atlas"
            org="Acme Inc."
            tagline="Sales and service reporting for every Acme store."
            image={~p"/images/sign-in.jpg"}
            href={~p"/auth/entra"}
            configured={@entra_configured}
            notice={Phoenix.Flash.get(@flash, :sign_in)}
          >
            <:development :if={@development?} label="Sign in as a role">
              <.form for={@form} action={~p"/sign-in/development"}>…</.form>
            </:development>
            <:footer><.link href={~p"/privacy"}>Privacy</.link></:footer>
          </.sign_in_page>
          <.flash_group flash={@flash} />
          '''
        }
      />
      <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
        A controller that refuses a sign-in, or signs someone out, puts the notice's key in the
        flash under <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm">:sign_in</code>
        and redirects to the sign-in page. The page words it, so every app says it the same way.
      </p>
      <.code_block
        language="elixir"
        code={
          ~S'''
          defp refuse(conn, reason) do
            conn |> put_flash(:sign_in, notice(reason)) |> redirect(to: ~p"/sign-in")
          end

          defp notice(reason) when reason in [:not_set_up, :no_app_role, :no_brand], do: "no_access"
          defp notice(:removed), do: "ended"
          defp notice(:entra_unavailable), do: "unavailable"
          defp notice(:canceled), do: "canceled"
          defp notice(:not_configured), do: "not_configured"
          defp notice(_bad_state_or_reply), do: "failed"

          def delete(conn, _params) do
            conn |> Auth.sign_out() |> put_flash(:sign_in, "signed_out") |> redirect(to: ~p"/sign-in")
          end
          '''
        }
      />
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Notices</h2>
      <div class="card w-full overflow-hidden">
        <table class="table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th class="w-36">Key</th>
              <th>Says</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr :for={{key, says} <- sign_in_notices()}>
              <td><code class="font-mono text-xs">{key}</code></td>
              <td class="text-sm">{says}</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
        <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm">
          configured=&lbrace;false&rbrace;
        </code>
        shows the not-set-up notice and disables the button. A key the page doesn't know shows
        nothing. Anything else is an
        <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm">
          &lt;:alert title="…"&gt;
        </code>
        of the app's own.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Development sign-in</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
        The
        <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm">&lt;:development&gt;</code>
        slot sits under a divider. The app renders it only in development and test builds, as it
        does the route behind it. Each entry with a
        <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm">label</code>
        is a section that folds away, and the whole development sign-in folds away too. The
        browser remembers what's hidden, so a developer can keep the page as production shows it.
      </p>
      <.preview_frame size="desktop" slug="development" />
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">The app's look</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
        The package stays neutral, and the app brings its look.
        <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm">image</code>
        fills the desktop panel and the page behind the tablet card, darkened so the text on it
        reads. The colours come from the theme: a brand theme's
        <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm">--sign-in-accent</code>
        runs through the application's name over the picture, and its primary colours the button
        and the mark. A brand scope
        (<code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm">data-brand</code>)
        brands just the sign-in page in an app that runs the neutral theme.
        <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm">&lt;:panel&gt;</code>
        replaces the panel's centre, and
        <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm">&lt;:logo&gt;</code>
        the icon tile over the form.
      </p>
      <.code_block
        language="css"
        code={
          ~S'''
          /* the brand theme's CSS: the whole app, or just the sign-in page */
          [data-theme="acme"], [data-theme="acme-dark"] { --sign-in-accent: var(--primary); }
          [data-brand="acme"] {
            --primary: oklch(0.62 0.19 260);
            --primary-foreground: oklch(0.985 0 0);
            --color-primary: var(--primary);
            --color-primary-content: var(--primary-foreground);
            --sign-in-accent: var(--primary);
          }
          '''
        }
      />
      <.code_block
        language="heex"
        code={
          ~S'''
          <.sign_in_page app_name="Atlas" image={~p"/images/sign-in.jpg"} data-brand="acme" …>
            <:panel>
              <p class="sign-in-app-name">Atlas</p>
              <span class="sign-in-rule"></span>
              <p class="sign-in-tagline">Reporting for every store<br /><strong>in one place</strong></p>
            </:panel>
          </.sign_in_page>
          '''
        }
      />
    </section>
  </div>
</.docs_layout>
